      "id": "7d7e4cad-581b-4557-8c0a-4b4868d5177f",
      "text": "**NAND** is an AND followed by NOT; **NOR** is an OR followed by NOT. The small output bubble means inversion.\n\n**XOR**, $A\\oplus B$, is 1 when the inputs differ. XNOR is 1 when they match. XOR is not ordinary OR: $1\\oplus1=0$.",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "answer": "Only A=B=1.",
      "citations": [],
      "difficulty": "intermediate",
      "id": "5bb38c1c-23d2-40bb-b5a9-7ca5442294d3",
      "origin": "original",
      "prompt": "For $F=A+B$ and $G=A\\oplus B$, find every input row where $F\\ne G$.",
      "solution": "",
      "steps": [
        {
          "explanation": "Both give 0 at 00 and 1 at 01 and 10.",
          "latex": ""
        },
        {
          "explanation": "At 11, OR remains 1 while XOR is 0.",
          "latex": ""
        }
      ],
      "title": "Try it: distinguish OR from XOR",
      "type": "practice_problem"
    },
