      "id": "07950187-2d59-4339-b3a9-8098dc78fac0",
      "text": "In **positive logic**, low voltage represents 0 and high voltage represents 1. A range between the valid low and high input levels is undefined; it is not a third valid binary value.",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "5e41de12-4bd1-4a73-bc38-3516d2e6c775",
          "source_id": "43433cc2-ac9b-4f48-9f8f-e352ed8b54e2",
          "version": 1
        }
      ],
      "columns": [
        "Quantity",
        "Meaning"
      ],
      "id": "98c83b07-c0c1-49ef-863b-889405c4ed04",
      "rows": [
        [
          "$V_{OL(\\max)}$",
          "Largest guaranteed low output voltage"
        ],
        [
          "$V_{OH(\\min)}$",
          "Smallest guaranteed high output voltage"
        ],
        [
          "$V_{IL(\\max)}$",
          "Largest voltage guaranteed to be accepted as a low input"
        ],
        [
          "$V_{IH(\\min)}$",
          "Smallest voltage guaranteed to be accepted as a high input"
        ]
      ],
      "type": "table"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
